# Milestone: M3
# Covers: nested tag scopes; stopping the outer tag cascades through the
#         inner scope's onleave handler; cleanup ordering is outer-then-inner
#         (row 7 §6.3 worked example).
#
# defer-to: M4/M5
#
# Reason: requires tag.stop() method-call syntax (M4 object model + method
# dispatch) and onleave clause parse/emit (M5 reactive runtime).  At M3,
# OP_PUSH_TAG / OP_POP_TAG are emitted but tag.stop() has no urbiscript
# surface — it is only callable via the C API (urbi_tag_stop).  The onleave
# keyword is not parsed at M3.
#
# When M4/M5 land, implement this fixture by uncommenting the source below.
# Expected behaviour: outer.stop() cascades through inner onleave first, then
# outer onleave; log ends up "io".
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at M4/M5):
#   var log = "";
#   var outer = Tag.new;
#   var inner = Tag.new;
#   outer: { inner: { 1 | outer.stop("done") | 2 } onleave { log = log + "i" } } onleave { log = log + "o" };
#   log
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] "io"
